---
/**
 * florist / PageBU — a dark floral atelier. Deep green night, Gloock display
 * over Manrope body, one champagne accent, hairline rules and square corners.
 * Fully self-contained, like hospitality/PageBJ: it shares nothing with the
 * older florist PageBR / FloristSpine files in this folder.
 *
 * ROLE OF THIS FILE: the wrapper emits the WHOLE document (doctype, head,
 * tokens, fonts, Leaflet css + js, skip link, map boot). It does NOT compose
 * with BaseLayout. It is the only file in the variant that touches `siteData`;
 * the sixteen section components receive only `layout` + `content`.
 *
 * EDITABLE HOOKS OWNED BY THIS FILE: none. It only READS layout.businessName /
 * layout.tagline (title), content.description (meta description),
 * layout.favicon and layout.ogImage. Every data-field / data-image-field /
 * data-href-field hook lives in a section component, with the design's exact
 * paths. Section visibility is the fourteen camelCase `visibility.*` keys
 * below, each tested `!== false` (undefined renders).
 *
 * THE ONE HARDCODED VISIBLE STRING is the skip link's "Skip to content"
 * (visible on focus only). The footer's "Follow" and the location rows'
 * Address / Hours / Phone labels are template chrome in their sections, each
 * gated on the value it labels.
 *
 * TOKEN PLAN (decided for a DARK design under the colour engine).
 *
 *   THE FIXED WORLD. The night greens and the two text tones live in names
 *   buildOverrideCss does not know, so an admin colour pick cannot touch them:
 *     --night  (page ground, hero panel, the label on every champagne fill)
 *     --night-2 (the raised bands, the mobile drawer, photo wells)
 *     --night-3 (photo wells inside a raised band, the closing-band hover)
 *     --night-4 (footer ground)   --cream (text)   --sage (secondary text)
 *   Why fixed: every light scheme the florist family offers (pink, purple,
 *   green, brown, whitegold) would otherwise turn this night page into a pale
 *   one, which is a different design — the mistake PageBJ had to undo and
 *   PageBK avoids the same way.
 *
 *   THE ONE MOVING PART is the champagne, declared as --accent-light plus
 *   --accent-rgb for its tints. Why --accent-light and not --accent: the
 *   engine writes palette.primary into --accent, a mid-tone tuned for LIGHT
 *   paper, which measures on this night 1.54 (maroon), 2.57 (brown), 3.40
 *   (pink), 3.97 (purple). --accent-light receives palette.accent, the
 *   scheme's light tint, which is the champagne's actual role here (a light
 *   accent on a dark ground): 7.53 pink, 6.18 purple, 9.65 green, 5.08 brown,
 *   8.87 whitegold, 2.37 maroon (maroon is the one scheme that breaks; see
 *   the report). --accent and the other engine aliases are declared with the
 *   champagne so an inherited rule finds a sane value, but no selector in
 *   this template reads --accent.
 *
 *   THE LABEL ON A CHAMPAGNE FILL is the fixed --night, not the engine's
 *   --on-accent. The engine picks that label by luminance with a 0.5
 *   threshold and returns white on the pink, purple and brown tints (2.23,
 *   2.72, 3.31:1), where the night holds 7.53, 6.18 and 5.08.
 *
 *   THE ONLY !important IN THIS TEMPLATE (one decision, three declarations).
 *   On any explicit pick buildOverrideCss also emits `html, body {
 *   background: var(--paper) !important; color: var(--ink) !important }`.
 *   Sections paint their own grounds, but the canvas (overscroll, and what
 *   the translucent sticky header shows at the top of the page) is html/body,
 *   so the html and body grounds and the body text colour are pinned to the
 *   night world here with a more specific !important. That keeps the fixed
 *   world whole under a pick.
 *
 * CONTRAST, native palette: cream/night 14.01, sage/night 8.93, sage/night-2
 * 7.88, champagne/night 9.84, champagne/night-2 8.68, night on champagne 9.84.
 *
 * FONT-PAIRING SENTINEL (two lines, wrapper-local): lib/astro-builder.ts
 * defaults layout.fontPairing to the literal 'modern' and lockVariant does not
 * blank it, so without the sentinel buildOverrideCss force-swaps Space
 * Grotesk + Inter onto nearly every real site. astro-builder's default is
 * treated as unset; a deliberate admin pick still applies.
 *
 * FORBIDDEN CLASS NAMES (buildOverrideCss pins them with !important):
 *   .btn-primary .btn-ghost .btn-yellow .btn-light .nav-cta .nav-right
 *   .testi .cta-band .trust, and `hero` as a class anywhere.
 * Buttons here are .btn with .btn--fill / .btn--line / .btn--quiet, the
 * closing band's own two variants, and .linkc for the directions link.
 *
 * DESIGN ISOLATION: every selector in the global block is anchored
 * html[data-page="BU"], including the reset, body, img, a and ::selection.
 * Base primitives are wrapped in :where() so an Astro-scoped section rule
 * (0,2,0) always beats them (0,1,1).
 *
 * RENDER ORDER, exactly as the design draws it: Header, Hero (#top), Marquee
 * (#marquee), Trust, Services (#services), About (#about), Why (#why), Gallery
 * (#gallery), How (#how), Testimonials (#reviews), Credentials (#credentials),
 * Area (#area), Faq (#faq), Location (#visit), then outside <main> the closing
 * band (#book) and the Footer, followed by the floating message pill.
 *
 * LEAFLET: this wrapper loads leaflet.css + leaflet.js and defines
 * window.__floristBUInitMap (family-unique). LocationBU calls that exact name,
 * or parks its arguments in window.__floristBUPending, which the boot script
 * drains right after defining the function (no timer can run out on a slow
 * leaflet.js download).
 * Keep `el.innerHTML = ''` in the boot, it erases the drawn fallback face, and
 * keep id="map" literal. Tiles are the design's own CARTO dark_all night map,
 * the same style PageBK uses; lib/carto.ts adds the key at publish.
 */
import HeaderBU from './header/HeaderBU.astro';
import HeroBU from './hero/HeroBU.astro';
import MarqueeBU from './marquee/MarqueeBU.astro';
import TrustBU from './trust/TrustBU.astro';
import ServicesBU from './services/ServicesBU.astro';
import AboutBU from './about/AboutBU.astro';
import WhyBU from './why/WhyBU.astro';
import GalleryBU from './gallery/GalleryBU.astro';
import HowBU from './how/HowBU.astro';
import TestimonialsBU from './testimonials/TestimonialsBU.astro';
import CredentialsBU from './credentials/CredentialsBU.astro';
import AreaBU from './area/AreaBU.astro';
import FaqBU from './faq/FaqBU.astro';
import LocationBU from './location/LocationBU.astro';
import CtaBandBU from './ctaBand/CtaBandBU.astro';
import FooterBU from './footer/FooterBU.astro';
import { resolveTheme, buildFontHref, buildOverrideCss } from '../../lib/genericThemeOverrides';

interface Props { siteData: any; }
const { siteData } = Astro.props;
const layout = siteData.layout ?? {};
const content = siteData.content ?? {};
const visibility = siteData.visibility ?? {};
const title = layout.businessName
  ? `${layout.businessName}${layout.tagline ? ' — ' + layout.tagline : ''}`
  : 'Welcome';
const { scheme: __themeScheme, pairing: __resolvedPairing } = resolveTheme(layout, (content as any).business_type, { lockVariant: true });
// 'modern' is astro-builder's DEFAULT, not a choice (lib/astro-builder.ts).
// Treating it as unset keeps Gloock + Manrope; a deliberate admin pick applies.
const __themePairing = __resolvedPairing === 'modern' ? '' : __resolvedPairing;
const __overrideCss = buildOverrideCss(__themeScheme, __themePairing);
const __fontHref = buildFontHref(__themePairing);
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" data-page="BU">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>{title}</title>
  {content.description && <meta name="description" content={content.description} />}
  <!-- Browser-chrome tint. A meta tag cannot read a CSS var, so this repeats
       the fixed --night ground the sticky header sits on. -->
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#13201A" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin="" />
  <!-- The design's own faces, verbatim from its helmet link: Gloock (one
       weight) for display, Manrope 400-700 for body and tracked caps. -->
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Gloock&family=Manrope:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.css" integrity="sha256-p4NxAoJBhIIN+hmNHrzRCf9tD/miZyoHS5obTRR9BMY=" crossorigin="" />
  {layout.favicon && <link rel="icon" href={layout.favicon} />}
  {(layout.ogImage || layout.favicon) && <meta property="og:image" content={layout.ogImage || layout.favicon} />}

  <style is:global>
    /* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       PageBU · florist · dark atelier. Tokens + shared base primitives. EVERY
       selector is anchored html[data-page="BU"] so nothing leaks into a sister
       wrapper, and nothing leaks in. Base primitives sit inside :where() so an
       Astro-scoped section rule always wins them.

       HEAD ORDER is load-bearing: this block, then the {__fontHref} link, then
       LAST the set:html override block. The engine's html:root !important
       only beats these tokens because it arrives later.
       (Never write a literal end-style tag in this block, comments included.)
    ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

    html[data-page="BU"] {
      /* ── THE FIXED WORLD. Names the override engine does not know, so an
            admin colour pick leaves the night alone (see the frontmatter). */
      --night: #13201A;
      --night-2: #1B2B23;
      --night-3: #24382D;
      --night-4: #0E1813;
      --cream: #EFEADF;
      --sage: #B9BFB2;
      --night-rgb: 19,32,26;
      --cream-rgb: 239,234,223;
      --sage-rgb: 185,191,178;

      /* ── THE ONE MOVING PART: the champagne. The engine rewrites these two
            with palette.accent / palette.accentRgb on an explicit pick. */
      --accent-light: #D8C49B;
      --accent-rgb: 216,196,155;

      /* ── The engine's own vocabulary, declared so any inherited rule finds
            a sane value. NO SELECTOR IN THIS TEMPLATE READS THESE. */
      --accent: #D8C49B;
      --accent-soft: #D8C49B;
      --accent-deep: #D8C49B;
      --paper: #13201A;
      --paper-2: #1B2B23;
      --card: #1B2B23;
      --ink: #EFEADF;
      --ink-soft: #B9BFB2;
      --line: #323C36;
      --muted: #B9BFB2;
      --paper-rgb: 19,32,26;
      --ink-rgb: 239,234,223;
      --on-accent: #13201A;
      --on-primary: #13201A;
      --on-ink: #13201A;
      --on-paper: #EFEADF;
      --on-brass: #13201A;

      /* ── type + metrics */
      --disp: "Gloock", Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
      --serif: "Gloock", Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
      --sans: "Manrope", system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      /* No monospace in this design; its tracked caps are Manrope 700. */
      --mono: "Manrope", system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      --maxw: 1320px;
      --gutter: clamp(18px,4vw,56px);
    }

    /* ── reset + document ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    html[data-page="BU"] *,
    html[data-page="BU"] *::before,
    html[data-page="BU"] *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
    html[data-page="BU"] {
      -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%;
      scroll-behavior: smooth;
      /* The sticky header is 79px; every in-page anchor lands clear of it. On
         the root rather than per section so FAQ rows and the map are covered
         and keyboard focus never hides under the rail. */
      scroll-padding-top: 90px;
      /* Pinned: see THE ONLY !important IN THIS TEMPLATE in the frontmatter. */
      background-color: var(--night) !important;
    }
    /* The fixed message pill (FooterBU's .fab, a sibling after </footer>)
       covers the bottom band of the viewport: up to 54px plus its 24px
       offset. When it renders, reserve that band too, so a keyboard-focused
       link or FAQ row is scrolled clear of the pill instead of under it
       (WCAG 2.4.11). Gated on the pill, so pages without one are unchanged. */
    html[data-page="BU"]:has(> body > a.fab) { scroll-padding-bottom: 88px; }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { html[data-page="BU"] { scroll-behavior: auto; } }
    html[data-page="BU"] body {
      margin: 0; padding: 0;
      background-color: var(--night) !important;
      color: var(--cream) !important;
      font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 16.5px; line-height: 1.7;
      -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; overflow-x: hidden;
      overflow-wrap: break-word;
    }
    html[data-page="BU"] main { display: block; background-color: var(--night); color: var(--cream); }
    /* Element resets sit at ZERO specificity (the whole selector inside
       :where), exactly as weak as the design's own bare `a {…}` reset. A
       bare `html[…] a` would score (0,1,2): it out-ranked every button
       primitive below and reset each label to the inherited colour, and it
       beat Leaflet's `.leaflet-bar a` / attribution link colours too. */
    :where(html[data-page="BU"] img) { max-width: 100%; display: block; }
    :where(html[data-page="BU"] a) { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
    /* The design's one global hover: an unstyled link turns champagne.
       Zero-specificity as well, so every control that styles its own hover
       (all of this template's, and Leaflet's) keeps it. */
    :where(html[data-page="BU"] a:hover) { color: var(--accent-light); }
    html[data-page="BU"] ::selection { background: var(--accent-light); color: var(--night); }
    /* text-transform is DECLARED, not defaulted: an unscoped uppercase heading
       rule from another template once reached every page through index.astro.
       No line-height here on purpose — the design's small headings inherit the
       page's 1.7, and each display heading sets its own. */
    html[data-page="BU"] :where(h1,h2,h3,h4) {
      margin: 0; font-family: var(--disp); font-weight: 400; color: inherit;
      letter-spacing: 0; text-transform: none;
    }
    html[data-page="BU"] :where(p, figure, blockquote, dl, dd) { margin: 0; }

    /* ── layout scaffolding: the design's 1320px column and fluid gutter ── */
    html[data-page="BU"] :where(.wrap) {
      max-width: var(--maxw);
      margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;
      padding-left: var(--gutter); padding-right: var(--gutter);
    }

    /* ── .kick — the eyebrow: 12px Manrope 700, .24em, champagne ────────── */
    html[data-page="BU"] :where(.kick) {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: .24em; text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--accent-light);
    }

    /* ── .h2 — the display headline, in the design's three sizes ─────────── */
    html[data-page="BU"] :where(.h2) {
      margin: 16px 0 0;
      font-family: var(--disp); font-weight: 400; color: var(--cream);
    }
    html[data-page="BU"] :where(.h2:first-child) { margin-top: 0; }
    html[data-page="BU"] :where(.h2--xl) { font-size: clamp(34px,4.8vw,66px); line-height: 1.04; }
    html[data-page="BU"] :where(.h2--lg) { font-size: clamp(32px,4.4vw,58px); line-height: 1.06; }
    html[data-page="BU"] :where(.h2--md) { font-size: clamp(32px,4.2vw,54px); line-height: 1.06; }

    /* ── BUTTONS. Square, tracked caps, a 1px border on every variant. Each
          variant declares its own fill and restates fill AND label on hover,
          straight from the design's style-hover attributes. No transition:
          the design swaps instantly. ───────────────────────────────────── */
    html[data-page="BU"] :where(.btn) {
      /* DECLARED, not left to chance: index.astro bundles every template's
         global CSS, so a control with no fill of its own takes whatever lands
         last. */
      background-color: transparent;
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
      min-height: 54px; padding: 0 30px;
      border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 0;
      font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; text-decoration: none;
      color: var(--cream); cursor: pointer;
    }
    /* champagne fill, night label; hover turns the fill cream */
    html[data-page="BU"] :where(.btn--fill) {
      background-color: var(--accent-light); border-color: var(--accent-light); color: var(--night);
    }
    html[data-page="BU"] :where(.btn--fill:hover) {
      background-color: var(--cream); border-color: var(--cream); color: var(--night);
    }
    /* champagne hairline, champagne label; hover fills champagne */
    html[data-page="BU"] :where(.btn--line) {
      background-color: transparent; border-color: var(--accent-light); color: var(--accent-light);
    }
    html[data-page="BU"] :where(.btn--line:hover) {
      background-color: var(--accent-light); border-color: var(--accent-light); color: var(--night);
    }
    /* the quiet secondary: cream label in a faint cream hairline */
    html[data-page="BU"] :where(.btn--quiet) {
      background-color: transparent; border-color: rgba(var(--cream-rgb),.4); color: var(--cream);
    }
    html[data-page="BU"] :where(.btn--quiet:hover) {
      background-color: transparent; border-color: var(--cream); color: var(--cream);
    }

    /* ── .linkc — the underlined text action (directions). Only the label
          colour moves on hover; the rule under it stays champagne. ───────── */
    html[data-page="BU"] :where(.linkc) {
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; min-height: 44px;
      font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--accent-light); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--accent-light);
    }
    html[data-page="BU"] :where(.linkc:hover) { color: var(--cream); }

    /* ── FOCUS. The design draws none, so one ring for everything: a cream
          outline clear of the control, legible on every night ground. The
          champagne closing band restates it in night. ─────────────────── */
    html[data-page="BU"] :where(a, button, summary, [tabindex]):focus-visible {
      outline: 2px solid var(--cream); outline-offset: 3px;
    }

    /* ── skip link (the one hardcoded visible string) ──────────────────── */
    html[data-page="BU"] :where(.skip) {
      position: absolute; left: -999px; top: 0; z-index: 100;
      background-color: var(--accent-light); color: var(--night);
      padding: 12px 18px;
      font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase;
    }
    html[data-page="BU"] :where(.skip:focus) { left: 0; top: 0; }
  </style>

  {__fontHref && <link href={__fontHref} rel="stylesheet" />}
  <style is:global set:html={__overrideCss}></style>
</head>
<body>
  <a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
  <HeaderBU layout={layout} content={content} />
  <main id="main">
    {visibility.heroSection !== false && <HeroBU content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.marqueeBlock !== false && <MarqueeBU content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.trustBlock !== false && <TrustBU content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.servicesSection !== false && <ServicesBU content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.aboutSection !== false && <AboutBU content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.whyUsBlock !== false && <WhyBU content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.gallerySection !== false && <GalleryBU content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.howItWorksBlock !== false && <HowBU content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.testimonialsBlock !== false && <TestimonialsBU content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.credentialsBlock !== false && <CredentialsBU content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.serviceAreaBlock !== false && <AreaBU content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.faqBlock !== false && <FaqBU content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.locationBlock !== false && <LocationBU content={content} layout={layout} />}
  </main>
  {visibility.ctaBandBlock !== false && <CtaBandBU content={content} layout={layout} />}
  <FooterBU layout={layout} content={content} />

  <script is:inline src="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.js" integrity="sha256-20nQCchB9co0qIjJZRGuk2/Z9VM+kNiyxNV1lvTlZBo=" crossorigin=""></script>
  <script is:inline>
    // florist / BU Leaflet boot. The global name is family-unique on purpose: a
    // preview harness can render two wrappers in one document, and a shared
    // name cross-wires the maps. LocationBU calls it with (lat, lng, label), or
    // — because its script runs BEFORE this one, and a slow leaflet.js can
    // hold this definition back for as long as the download takes — parks the
    // arguments in window.__floristBUPending, drained at the bottom of this
    // script. No timer on either side, so a slow CDN only delays the map.
    window.__floristBUInitMap = function (lat, lng, label) {
      var tries = 0;
      (function go() {
        var el = document.getElementById('map');
        if (!el || el.__buMap) return;
        // leaflet.js is a parser-blocking tag above, so by the time this runs
        // L exists — unless leaflet.js FAILED (blocked, offline, integrity
        // mismatch). This short retry only guards a document that runs the
        // boot out of order; giving up leaves the drawn fallback face, which
        // is a perfectly good thing to be left with.
        if (typeof window.L === 'undefined') { if (tries++ < 25) setTimeout(go, 80); return; }
        // Erases LocationBU's drawn fallback face; without it the tiles stack
        // on top of the drawn grid.
        el.innerHTML = '';
        var map = window.L.map(el, { scrollWheelZoom: false }).setView([lat, lng], 16);
        el.__buMap = map;
        // The design's own night basemap (CARTO dark_all, as PageBK). The
        // URL keeps the shape lib/carto.ts rewrites, so the key is added at
        // publish time.
        window.L.tileLayer('https://{s}.basemaps.cartocdn.com/dark_all/{z}/{x}/{y}{r}.png', {
          attribution: '&copy; OpenStreetMap &copy; CARTO', maxZoom: 19, subdomains: 'abcd'
        }).addTo(map);
        // The design's pin: an 18px champagne dot in a 5px champagne halo.
        // Colours are READ from the live tokens, so an explicit admin colour
        // pick recolours the pin too (the engine sets them on html:root).
        var cs = window.getComputedStyle(document.documentElement);
        var champ = (cs.getPropertyValue('--accent-light') || '').trim() || '#D8C49B';
        var rgb = (cs.getPropertyValue('--accent-rgb') || '').trim() || '216,196,155';
        var icon = window.L.divIcon({
          className: '',
          html: '<div style="width:18px;height:18px;border-radius:50%;background:' + champ + ';box-shadow:0 0 0 5px rgba(' + rgb + ',.25)"></div>',
          iconSize: [18, 18], iconAnchor: [9, 9]
        });
        // No popup and no tooltip: the design's pin carries neither. The map
        // node itself is labelled (role="img" + aria-label in LocationBU).
        window.L.marker([lat, lng], { icon: icon, keyboard: false }).addTo(map);
      })();
    };
    // Drain LocationBU's parked call (see above).
    (function () {
      var p = window.__floristBUPending;
      if (!p) return;
      window.__floristBUPending = null;
      window.__floristBUInitMap(p[0], p[1], p[2]);
    })();
  </script>
</body>
</html>
